# dctx Global Omit Content Rules
#
# Files matching these patterns will APPEAR in the directory tree
# but their CONTENT will be omitted from the output.
#
# Use this for files that are useful to know exist, but whose
# contents are too large or not useful for LLM context.
#
# Syntax: Same as .gitignore
# - One pattern per line
# - Lines starting with # are comments
# - Use ! to negate a pattern
# - Supports wildcards (* and **)
#
# Examples:
#   *.svg                - Omit content of SVG files (but show in tree)
#   package-lock.json    - Omit lockfile content
#   !critical.svg        - But include critical.svg content
#
# Default rules:

# SVG files (often large/unreadable XML)
*.svg

# Package manager lockfiles (verbose, auto-generated)
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
Cargo.lock
go.sum
Gemfile.lock
poetry.lock
Pipfile.lock
